<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ fund managers report a bumper June qtr - W.Mercer.</title>
<headline>NZ fund managers report a bumper June qtr - W.Mercer.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand investment managers had a bumper June quarter thanks to a stunning return in overseas shares and good performances in New Zealand shares and property, William Mercer reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Rates of return before tax and expenses ranged from 6.6 percent (Colonial Investment Management) to 11.0 percent (AMP Investments) with a the median return being 9.2 percent.</p>
<p>It said superannuation funds with a June year should be able to report very strong returns -- ranging from 15.5 percent (Colonial Investment Management) to 23.9 percent (ANZFM).  </p>
<p>W.Mercer expects over half of all funds have earned a gross rate of return of over 20 percent for the year.</p>
</text>
